# Accepted text-check findings. One entry per line:
#   rule | file pattern | word (optional) | reason
# The rule is required and cannot be *. tools/text_check.py has the rules.

# Words that the checker reads as an -ing verb or a passive, but that are
# nouns, names or adjectives here.
ing-form | hat/*.lua | pruning | a noun: the pruning of the descent
ing-form | * | rounding | a noun: correct rounding in IEEE-754
ing-form | mod/surface.lua | assembling | the name of the assembling machine
ing-form | * | tiling | a noun: the hat tiling
passive | * | are exempt | an adjective: rails are exempt from the band rule
passive | * | are permanent | an adjective: the bands are permanent
passive | * | is red | an adjective: the build preview is red
passive | * | is intended | an adjective: a game-design choice that is intended
ing-form | * | mining | the name of the mining drill
ing-form | docs/design/hattorio-design.md | starting | the name of the starting area

# The plans follow the writing-plans format ("Modify:" and "Verify" in the
# steps).
word | docs/plans/*.md | modify | the writing-plans file-list format
word | docs/plans/*.md | verify | the writing-plans step format

# The released entries of the changelog stay as they were published.
semicolon | CHANGELOG.md | | released entries, kept as published
passive | CHANGELOG.md | | released entries, kept as published

# A heading that names a topic, not an action.
ing-form | CLAUDE.md | writing | a heading that names the topic
ing-form | wiki/The-mathematics.md | floating | the term floating point
ing-form | wiki/_Sidebar.md | playing | a heading that names the topic
ing-form | wiki/Building-in-hats.md | crossing | a heading that names the topic
ing-form | tools/README.md | previewing | a heading that names the topic
